+    fine, because that graph consumes the whole context in one shot and never reads a cache. A draft
+    head does read one, every step after the first, and the encodings collected here are copied onto
+    the DECODE and PREFILL graphs. Calibrating with no cache therefore hands the deployed graph
+    quantization parameters for a tensor it never observed, which shows up as a run that is correct
+    on step 0 and degrades from step 1.
